vendor/
# Re-include the reveal.js decks' vendored runtime. These are small text assets
# (reveal.js + reveal.css) that the published decks load at runtime — if they
# are ignored, GitHub Pages builds without them and every deck renders BLANK.
# Verified failure mode, not hypothetical. Directory must be un-ignored before
# its contents can be.
!web-foundations/docs/tracks/**/vendor/
!web-foundations/docs/tracks/**/vendor/**

# Exam Forge + course-private material (banks, LMS exports, legacy private/)
private/
private/*
# Explicit (covered by private/ above; documented for portability to other repos)
# private/exams/
# private/exams-out/

# SQLite databases (local/dev artifacts)
*.db
*.db-*

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GOLD RULE — no binaries or source documents in this repository, ever.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This repo is TEXT: lessons, tracks, data files, configuration, small vendored
# text runtimes. It is not a document store and not a media library.
#
# Rationale:
#   1. COPYRIGHT — research PDFs, books and papers are licensed to the reader,
#      not redistributable. A public teaching repo must not host them.
#   2. PROVENANCE — scholarly sources live in Ahmes vaults
#      (~/ahmes-library/scholar/documents/<slug>_<hash8>/), which are the
#      sovereign, citable copy. Duplicating a PDF here creates a second,
#      unversioned truth.
#   3. SIZE — git stores binaries badly; every revision is a full new blob.
#   4. STUDENT DATA — coursework artefacts may contain personal data (RGPD).
#
# Anything below requires EXPLICIT human acceptance before being committed.
# To add one deliberately: `git add -f <path>` and say why in the commit body.
# Never bypass this with a broad `git add -A`.

# Documents & ebooks
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw3
*.djvu
*.ps

# Office / authoring formats
*.doc
*.docx
*.odt
*.rtf
*.ppt
*.pptx
